 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Try saying something like, I know you mean well, but some of your ideas aren't useful. Then ask her for specific examples and why she thinks they're unhelpful. I' being sincere. Asking for the evidence puts her on notice that you're not a kid anymore. Then lead with that. Say you appreciate her being interested in you, but you'd rather she ask how you're doing instead of lecturing you on organizing. Probably, if you lead with the vulnerable bit. People react well to that. Then ask if you can help, or at least agree before she starts. Then ask her to agree before she starts, so it feels like a plan together. She might not, but it' worth a shot. Family dynamics are tricky.",
